{"exhaustive":{"nbHits":false,"typo":false},"exhaustiveNbHits":false,"exhaustiveTypo":false,"hits":[{"_highlightResult":{"author":{"matchLevel":"none","matchedWords":[],"value":"rmxt"},"comment_text":{"fullyHighlighted":false,"matchLevel":"full","matchedWords":["agent"],"value":"Correction: There is a small chance that the celebrity/politician's publicity <em>agent</em> will tweet back at you. There is an even smaller chance the celebrity will tweet back at you.<p>I think that this is part of the reason why it's really the &quot;illusion of engagement&quot; and not <i>real</i> engagement. The elite will perpetually be separated from the masses... the specific medium may change, but the separation will persist."},"story_title":{"matchLevel":"none","matchedWords":[],"value":"Twitter\u2019s stock falls toward IPO-level prices"},"story_url":{"matchLevel":"none","matchedWords":[],"value":"http://techcrunch.com/2015/08/03/twitter-collapses-5-tumbling-toward-ipo-level-prices/"}},"_tags":["comment","author_rmxt","story_9998011"],"author":"rmxt","children":[10000606],"comment_text":"Correction: There is a small chance that the celebrity&#x2F;politician&#x27;s publicity agent will tweet back at you. There is an even smaller chance the celebrity will tweet back at you.<p>I think that this is part of the reason why it&#x27;s really the &quot;illusion of engagement&quot; and not <i>real</i> engagement. The elite will perpetually be separated from the masses... the specific medium may change, but the separation will persist.","created_at":"2015-08-03T21:29:01Z","created_at_i":1438637341,"objectID":"9999970","parent_id":9998991,"points":null,"story_id":9998011,"story_title":"Twitter\u2019s stock falls toward IPO-level prices","story_url":"http://techcrunch.com/2015/08/03/twitter-collapses-5-tumbling-toward-ipo-level-prices/","updated_at":"2023-09-07T03:22:05Z"},{"_highlightResult":{"author":{"matchLevel":"none","matchedWords":[],"value":"ato"},"comment_text":{"fullyHighlighted":false,"matchLevel":"full","matchedWords":["agent"],"value":"Indeed, perhaps it would be a better way to model the problem, I considered it but perhaps rejected it incorrectly.  By default Clojure uses a thread-pool for atoms so it wouldn't be a new thread for each request, the overhead is just a queue push which is not that great.  It would mean serializing all the updates, but you could use fine-grained <em>agent</em>s like I'm using fine-grained atoms."},"story_title":{"matchLevel":"none","matchedWords":[],"value":"Ongoing \u00b7 Concur.next \u2014 Hard-Core Clojure"},"story_url":{"matchLevel":"none","matchedWords":[],"value":"http://www.tbray.org/ongoing/When/200x/2009/12/15/Osborne-WF2-Clojure"}},"_tags":["comment","author_ato","story_998796"],"author":"ato","comment_text":"Indeed, perhaps it would be a better way to model the problem, I considered it but perhaps rejected it incorrectly.  By default Clojure uses a thread-pool for atoms so it wouldn't be a new thread for each request, the overhead is just a queue push which is not that great.  It would mean serializing all the updates, but you could use fine-grained agents like I'm using fine-grained atoms.","created_at":"2009-12-16T23:03:13Z","created_at_i":1261004593,"objectID":"999945","parent_id":998875,"story_id":998796,"story_title":"Ongoing \u00b7 Concur.next \u2014 Hard-Core Clojure","story_url":"http://www.tbray.org/ongoing/When/200x/2009/12/15/Osborne-WF2-Clojure","updated_at":"2024-09-19T16:53:57Z"},{"_highlightResult":{"author":{"matchLevel":"none","matchedWords":[],"value":"wtallis"},"comment_text":{"fullyHighlighted":false,"matchLevel":"full","matchedWords":["agent"],"value":"On the web, fine print policies don't matter in the end. You can fuss about them in court, but ultimately what matters is whether you send the data the other party requests.<p>If you as a user let your user <em>agent</em> send identifying information to sites that request it, you bear some responsibility for that. If you as a server operator configure your server to send content without first requiring identification and authentication, then you're putting it out there for the public to consume.<p>Any trusting of the other party (client trusting the server to not abuse information collected, server trusting client to also fetch and display ads from third-parties) is going to be imperfect. The servers have largely proven themselves to be untrustworthy in general, but they still mostly trust the client. As users wise up and start exercising their power over their own computers, the server operators will have to compensate by first squeezing the most value they can out of the users who are too trusting, but then by actually charging money. There's simply no other end-game possible unless someone figures out how to prevent servers from being untrustworthy in the first place."},"story_title":{"matchLevel":"none","matchedWords":[],"value":"EFF, AdBlock and Others Launch New \u201cDo Not Track\u201d Standard"},"story_url":{"matchLevel":"none","matchedWords":[],"value":"https://threatpost.com/eff-adblock-and-others-launch-new-do-not-track-standard/114121"}},"_tags":["comment","author_wtallis","story_9997533"],"author":"wtallis","comment_text":"On the web, fine print policies don&#x27;t matter in the end. You can fuss about them in court, but ultimately what matters is whether you send the data the other party requests.<p>If you as a user let your user agent send identifying information to sites that request it, you bear some responsibility for that. If you as a server operator configure your server to send content without first requiring identification and authentication, then you&#x27;re putting it out there for the public to consume.<p>Any trusting of the other party (client trusting the server to not abuse information collected, server trusting client to also fetch and display ads from third-parties) is going to be imperfect. The servers have largely proven themselves to be untrustworthy in general, but they still mostly trust the client. As users wise up and start exercising their power over their own computers, the server operators will have to compensate by first squeezing the most value they can out of the users who are too trusting, but then by actually charging money. There&#x27;s simply no other end-game possible unless someone figures out how to prevent servers from being untrustworthy in the first place.","created_at":"2015-08-03T19:24:46Z","created_at_i":1438629886,"objectID":"9999111","parent_id":9998925,"points":null,"story_id":9997533,"story_title":"EFF, AdBlock and Others Launch New \u201cDo Not Track\u201d Standard","story_url":"https://threatpost.com/eff-adblock-and-others-launch-new-do-not-track-standard/114121","updated_at":"2023-09-07T03:22:05Z"},{"_highlightResult":{"author":{"matchLevel":"none","matchedWords":[],"value":"tedsanders"},"comment_text":{"fullyHighlighted":false,"matchLevel":"full","matchedWords":["agent"],"value":"Obviously a single tech support <em>agent</em> being wrong about Microsoft's policy is not news.<p>From what Microsoft has said, it sounds like a new motherboard will require a new copy of Windows 10, but other hardware upgrades will not.<p><a href=\"http://answers.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/forum/windows_10-win_upgrade/reinstalling-windows-10-after-upgrade/578d0b7f-57e4-4893-b9d1-6cfac0d6290a?auth=1\" rel=\"nofollow\">http://answers.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/forum/windows_10-...</a>"},"story_title":{"matchLevel":"none","matchedWords":[],"value":"Windows 10 will not permit re-installation if any hardware changes"},"story_url":{"matchLevel":"none","matchedWords":[],"value":"http://imgur.com/gallery/8OJ4t"}},"_tags":["comment","author_tedsanders","story_9998973"],"author":"tedsanders","comment_text":"Obviously a single tech support agent being wrong about Microsoft&#x27;s policy is not news.<p>From what Microsoft has said, it sounds like a new motherboard will require a new copy of Windows 10, but other hardware upgrades will not.<p><a href=\"http:&#x2F;&#x2F;answers.microsoft.com&#x2F;en-us&#x2F;windows&#x2F;forum&#x2F;windows_10-win_upgrade&#x2F;reinstalling-windows-10-after-upgrade&#x2F;578d0b7f-57e4-4893-b9d1-6cfac0d6290a?auth=1\" rel=\"nofollow\">http:&#x2F;&#x2F;answers.microsoft.com&#x2F;en-us&#x2F;windows&#x2F;forum&#x2F;windows_10-...</a>","created_at":"2015-08-03T19:24:14Z","created_at_i":1438629854,"objectID":"9999106","parent_id":9998973,"points":null,"story_id":9998973,"story_title":"Windows 10 will not permit re-installation if any hardware changes","story_url":"http://imgur.com/gallery/8OJ4t","updated_at":"2023-09-07T03:22:05Z"},{"_highlightResult":{"author":{"matchLevel":"none","matchedWords":[],"value":"gruez"},"comment_text":{"fullyHighlighted":false,"matchLevel":"full","matchedWords":["agent"],"value":"I feel that the methodology of that site reports your browser as more unique than it really is. For one, it doesn't take into account that plugins/browsers are constantly getting updated. This causes the user-<em>agent</em> string and the plugin names to constantly change, causing the site to report more entropy than there really is. For instance, I'm using firefox on windows 8.1. Based on the market share of windows 8.1 (13%) and firefox (11%), the chance that another browser has the same user-<em>agent</em> should be 1 in 70. However panopticlick reports 1 in 943.29. Similarly, panopticlick reports that 1 in 7596.81 uses the latest version of the NPAPI flash plugin."},"story_title":{"matchLevel":"none","matchedWords":[],"value":"EFF, AdBlock and Others Launch New \u201cDo Not Track\u201d Standard"},"story_url":{"matchLevel":"none","matchedWords":[],"value":"https://threatpost.com/eff-adblock-and-others-launch-new-do-not-track-standard/114121"}},"_tags":["comment","author_gruez","story_9997533"],"author":"gruez","children":[9998318,9998340,9998345],"comment_text":"I feel that the methodology of that site reports your browser as more unique than it really is. For one, it doesn&#x27;t take into account that plugins&#x2F;browsers are constantly getting updated. This causes the user-agent string and the plugin names to constantly change, causing the site to report more entropy than there really is. For instance, I&#x27;m using firefox on windows 8.1. Based on the market share of windows 8.1 (13%) and firefox (11%), the chance that another browser has the same user-agent should be 1 in 70. However panopticlick reports 1 in 943.29. Similarly, panopticlick reports that 1 in 7596.81 uses the latest version of the NPAPI flash plugin.","created_at":"2015-08-03T17:33:22Z","created_at_i":1438623202,"objectID":"9998049","parent_id":9997845,"points":null,"story_id":9997533,"story_title":"EFF, AdBlock and Others Launch New \u201cDo Not Track\u201d Standard","story_url":"https://threatpost.com/eff-adblock-and-others-launch-new-do-not-track-standard/114121","updated_at":"2023-09-07T03:21:59Z"},{"_highlightResult":{"author":{"matchLevel":"none","matchedWords":[],"value":"chrisconley"},"comment_text":{"fullyHighlighted":false,"matchLevel":"full","matchedWords":["agent"],"value":"RealScout - Rails Engineers/Front-end Engineers/Data Engineers/Data Scientists - Mountain View, CA - Full-time<p>We pair program [1], hold hack days every other Friday [2], and have recently improved test coverage from 45% to 80%. The focus seems to be paying off: In the first half of 2015, our <em>agent</em>s have closed $1.1 billion in sales and this number is growing quickly.<p>(Check out our latest hack days project we released last week: an Atmel AVR 8bit microchip emulator [3] built with Rust, React.js, Redux.js and Docker.)<p>We're on the way to Series B being previously backed by Joe Lonsdale (Palantir founder), Ken DeLeon (2012's #1 Realtor) and several others ($7m to date)<p>If you're interested in helping to shape and mold engineering culture and technology in a small and growing team, feel free to reach me at chris (at) realscout.com.<p>-Chris<p>[1] - <a href=\"http://eatcodeplay.com/why-we-killed-off-code-reviews/\" rel=\"nofollow\">http://eatcodeplay.com/why-we-killed-off-code-reviews/</a><p>[2] - <a href=\"https://twitter.com/chrisconley/status/618830194971774976\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://twitter.com/chrisconley/status/618830194971774976</a><p>[3] - <a href=\"http://realscout.github.io/avr-emulator/\" rel=\"nofollow\">http://realscout.github.io/avr-emulator/</a>"},"story_title":{"matchLevel":"none","matchedWords":[],"value":"Ask HN: Who is hiring? (August 2015)"}},"_tags":["comment","author_chrisconley","story_9996333"],"author":"chrisconley","comment_text":"RealScout - Rails Engineers&#x2F;Front-end Engineers&#x2F;Data Engineers&#x2F;Data Scientists - Mountain View, CA - Full-time<p>We pair program [1], hold hack days every other Friday [2], and have recently improved test coverage from 45% to 80%. The focus seems to be paying off: In the first half of 2015, our agents have closed $1.1 billion in sales and this number is growing quickly.<p>(Check out our latest hack days project we released last week: an Atmel AVR 8bit microchip emulator [3] built with Rust, React.js, Redux.js and Docker.)<p>We&#x27;re on the way to Series B being previously backed by Joe Lonsdale (Palantir founder), Ken DeLeon (2012&#x27;s #1 Realtor) and several others ($7m to date)<p>If you&#x27;re interested in helping to shape and mold engineering culture and technology in a small and growing team, feel free to reach me at chris (at) realscout.com.<p>-Chris<p>[1] - <a href=\"http:&#x2F;&#x2F;eatcodeplay.com&#x2F;why-we-killed-off-code-reviews&#x2F;\" rel=\"nofollow\">http:&#x2F;&#x2F;eatcodeplay.com&#x2F;why-we-killed-off-code-reviews&#x2F;</a><p>[2] - <a href=\"https:&#x2F;&#x2F;twitter.com&#x2F;chrisconley&#x2F;status&#x2F;618830194971774976\" rel=\"nofollow\">https:&#x2F;&#x2F;twitter.com&#x2F;chrisconley&#x2F;status&#x2F;618830194971774976</a><p>[3] - <a href=\"http:&#x2F;&#x2F;realscout.github.io&#x2F;avr-emulator&#x2F;\" rel=\"nofollow\">http:&#x2F;&#x2F;realscout.github.io&#x2F;avr-emulator&#x2F;</a>","created_at":"2015-08-03T16:59:23Z","created_at_i":1438621163,"objectID":"9997719","parent_id":9996333,"story_id":9996333,"story_title":"Ask HN: Who is hiring? (August 2015)","updated_at":"2024-09-19T22:14:39Z"},{"_highlightResult":{"author":{"matchLevel":"none","matchedWords":[],"value":"jameincke"},"comment_text":{"fullyHighlighted":false,"matchLevel":"full","matchedWords":["agent"],"value":"CloserIQ (<a href=\"https://closeriq.com\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://closeriq.com</a>) | New York, NY<p>CloserIQ is the network connecting top sales talent to venture backed tech startups. We are a self-funded and highly profitable recruiting tech startup combining powerful software with world class service.<p>We are currently hiring for two roles:<p>Talent Advisor: <a href=\"http://clsr.us/jYihA/8bd29\" rel=\"nofollow\">http://clsr.us/jYihA/8bd29</a><p>Our Talent Advisors attract, engage and onboard top sales talent to the rapidly growing CloserIQ network. You\u2019ll be joining a small team of sales leaders, technologists, and growth hackers as a \u201csports <em>agent</em>\u201d for the top revenue generators in the tech community.<p>Business Operations Intern: <a href=\"http://clsr.us/j8h2w/8bd29\" rel=\"nofollow\">http://clsr.us/j8h2w/8bd29</a><p>We're looking for smart and tech savvy interns to help out as we grow the business. We're a team of 6 based in midtown east. You'll work with our founders, talent team and engineers on all aspects of the business and have a meaningful impact on the success of the company."},"story_title":{"matchLevel":"none","matchedWords":[],"value":"Ask HN: Who is hiring? (August 2015)"}},"_tags":["comment","author_jameincke","story_9996333"],"author":"jameincke","comment_text":"CloserIQ (<a href=\"https:&#x2F;&#x2F;closeriq.com\" rel=\"nofollow\">https:&#x2F;&#x2F;closeriq.com</a>) | New York, NY<p>CloserIQ is the network connecting top sales talent to venture backed tech startups. We are a self-funded and highly profitable recruiting tech startup combining powerful software with world class service.<p>We are currently hiring for two roles:<p>Talent Advisor: <a href=\"http:&#x2F;&#x2F;clsr.us&#x2F;jYihA&#x2F;8bd29\" rel=\"nofollow\">http:&#x2F;&#x2F;clsr.us&#x2F;jYihA&#x2F;8bd29</a><p>Our Talent Advisors attract, engage and onboard top sales talent to the rapidly growing CloserIQ network. You\u2019ll be joining a small team of sales leaders, technologists, and growth hackers as a \u201csports agent\u201d for the top revenue generators in the tech community.<p>Business Operations Intern: <a href=\"http:&#x2F;&#x2F;clsr.us&#x2F;j8h2w&#x2F;8bd29\" rel=\"nofollow\">http:&#x2F;&#x2F;clsr.us&#x2F;j8h2w&#x2F;8bd29</a><p>We&#x27;re looking for smart and tech savvy interns to help out as we grow the business. We&#x27;re a team of 6 based in midtown east. You&#x27;ll work with our founders, talent team and engineers on all aspects of the business and have a meaningful impact on the success of the company.","created_at":"2015-08-03T16:09:51Z","created_at_i":1438618191,"objectID":"9997153","parent_id":9996333,"story_id":9996333,"story_title":"Ask HN: Who is hiring? (August 2015)","updated_at":"2024-09-19T22:14:39Z"},{"_highlightResult":{"author":{"matchLevel":"none","matchedWords":[],"value":"hgh"},"comment_text":{"fullyHighlighted":false,"matchLevel":"full","matchedWords":["agent"],"value":"Zoona | Cape Town | <a href=\"http://www.ilovezoona.com\" rel=\"nofollow\">http://www.ilovezoona.com</a><p>Zoona helps people send and receive money when they need to most so that communities can thrive.  We have built a network of local entrepreneurs in Zambia and Malawi that manage 1000 retail locations providing services to over 400,000 consumers every month.  We are now looking to continue our expansion across Africa and diversify our product mix.<p>With Zoona you'll have an opportunity to join a great team and create real positive impact through your work.  You'll be able to live in beautiful Cape Town, and if you're not from here, we're happy to support relocation.<p>We're looking for:<p>* Frontend Developer.  Build out our client side using React and Backbone, while keeping a sharp focus on the customer experience for our <em>agent</em>s and consumers.<p>* Java Developer.  Contribute to and scale our core transaction platform and data analytics infrastructure.<p>* System Architect.  Take a lead role in defining and implementing our technology development plan across the stack.<p>For more information, please get in touch and I'll be happy to answer any questions - hans@ilovezoona.com"},"story_title":{"matchLevel":"none","matchedWords":[],"value":"Ask HN: Who is hiring? (August 2015)"}},"_tags":["comment","author_hgh","story_9996333"],"author":"hgh","comment_text":"Zoona | Cape Town | <a href=\"http:&#x2F;&#x2F;www.ilovezoona.com\" rel=\"nofollow\">http:&#x2F;&#x2F;www.ilovezoona.com</a><p>Zoona helps people send and receive money when they need to most so that communities can thrive.  We have built a network of local entrepreneurs in Zambia and Malawi that manage 1000 retail locations providing services to over 400,000 consumers every month.  We are now looking to continue our expansion across Africa and diversify our product mix.<p>With Zoona you&#x27;ll have an opportunity to join a great team and create real positive impact through your work.  You&#x27;ll be able to live in beautiful Cape Town, and if you&#x27;re not from here, we&#x27;re happy to support relocation.<p>We&#x27;re looking for:<p>* Frontend Developer.  Build out our client side using React and Backbone, while keeping a sharp focus on the customer experience for our agents and consumers.<p>* Java Developer.  Contribute to and scale our core transaction platform and data analytics infrastructure.<p>* System Architect.  Take a lead role in defining and implementing our technology development plan across the stack.<p>For more information, please get in touch and I&#x27;ll be happy to answer any questions - hans@ilovezoona.com","created_at":"2015-08-03T15:38:27Z","created_at_i":1438616307,"objectID":"9996780","parent_id":9996333,"story_id":9996333,"story_title":"Ask HN: Who is hiring? (August 2015)","updated_at":"2024-09-19T22:14:33Z"},{"_highlightResult":{"author":{"matchLevel":"none","matchedWords":[],"value":"stephengillie"},"comment_text":{"fullyHighlighted":false,"matchLevel":"full","matchedWords":["agent"],"value":"The connection kept resetting for me, so here is the Google Cache link: \n<a href=\"http://webcache.googleusercontent.com/search?q=cache:f-pnPOuBD-wJ:https://jakearchibald.com/2015/if-we-stand-still-we-go-backwards/+&amp;cd=1&amp;hl=en&amp;ct=clnk&amp;gl=us\" rel=\"nofollow\">http://webcache.googleusercontent.com/search?q=cache:f-pnPOu...</a><p>---<p>I don't web develop often. As a user, mobile web is usually more usable than a native app - not in terms of whether or not it works, but in terms of usability, flow of actions, and predictability. Cut, copy, and paste work in the browser but rarely in native apps. Other little things too, items too little for a project architect to notice or a punch list to pick up.<p>The other half of what killed Blackberry was Microsoft Activesync. Blackberry's email service required you have set up their Blackberry Enterprise Server (or their lower-performing cloud-hosted Blackberry Internet Service) and connected this to your email account. BES had an &quot;<em>agent</em>&quot;: a service that would log into your email account every 30 seconds, check for new email, and then forward this to your Blackberry over the Blackberry network (which is why you had to pay the $10 &quot;Blackberry Fee&quot;). Activesync (I think) used Exchange mail rules to do the same thing, and the iPhone mail client could use Activesync.<p>It was that &quot;one-two punch&quot; that took out Blackberry:<p><pre><code>  * iPhones were cool. Androids were cheap.\n  * Activesync comes with Exchange, no other server setup necessary. \n  * Works with normal carrier service; no $10 Blackberry fee.</code></pre>"},"story_title":{"matchLevel":"none","matchedWords":[],"value":"If we stand still, we go backwards"},"story_url":{"matchLevel":"none","matchedWords":[],"value":"https://jakearchibald.com/2015/if-we-stand-still-we-go-backwards/"}},"_tags":["comment","author_stephengillie","story_9995362"],"author":"stephengillie","children":[9996504,9997551],"comment_text":"The connection kept resetting for me, so here is the Google Cache link: \n<a href=\"http:&#x2F;&#x2F;webcache.googleusercontent.com&#x2F;search?q=cache:f-pnPOuBD-wJ:https:&#x2F;&#x2F;jakearchibald.com&#x2F;2015&#x2F;if-we-stand-still-we-go-backwards&#x2F;+&amp;cd=1&amp;hl=en&amp;ct=clnk&amp;gl=us\" rel=\"nofollow\">http:&#x2F;&#x2F;webcache.googleusercontent.com&#x2F;search?q=cache:f-pnPOu...</a><p>---<p>I don&#x27;t web develop often. As a user, mobile web is usually more usable than a native app - not in terms of whether or not it works, but in terms of usability, flow of actions, and predictability. Cut, copy, and paste work in the browser but rarely in native apps. Other little things too, items too little for a project architect to notice or a punch list to pick up.<p>The other half of what killed Blackberry was Microsoft Activesync. Blackberry&#x27;s email service required you have set up their Blackberry Enterprise Server (or their lower-performing cloud-hosted Blackberry Internet Service) and connected this to your email account. BES had an &quot;agent&quot;: a service that would log into your email account every 30 seconds, check for new email, and then forward this to your Blackberry over the Blackberry network (which is why you had to pay the $10 &quot;Blackberry Fee&quot;). Activesync (I think) used Exchange mail rules to do the same thing, and the iPhone mail client could use Activesync.<p>It was that &quot;one-two punch&quot; that took out Blackberry:<p><pre><code>  * iPhones were cool. Androids were cheap.\n  * Activesync comes with Exchange, no other server setup necessary. \n  * Works with normal carrier service; no $10 Blackberry fee.</code></pre>","created_at":"2015-08-03T15:09:51Z","created_at_i":1438614591,"objectID":"9996446","parent_id":9995362,"story_id":9995362,"story_title":"If we stand still, we go backwards","story_url":"https://jakearchibald.com/2015/if-we-stand-still-we-go-backwards/","updated_at":"2024-09-19T22:14:33Z"},{"_highlightResult":{"author":{"fullyHighlighted":false,"matchLevel":"full","matchedWords":["agent"],"value":"<em>agent</em>inbox"},"comment_text":{"fullyHighlighted":false,"matchLevel":"full","matchedWords":["agent"],"value":"<em>Agent</em> Inbox | <a href=\"http://agentinbox.com\" rel=\"nofollow\">http://<em>agent</em>inbox.com</a> | Remote (US Based)<p>Product Manager<p><em>Agent</em> Inbox is transforming the way real estate <em>agent</em>s transact business and communicate with one another. We have automated the messaging, scheduling, routing, and other parts of the real estate transaction. We are a product-driven company that is obsessed with the user experience and delighting our customers. We are having tremendous success in our initial markets, have a huge sales pipeline, and are aiming to grow fast.<p>We are looking for a world-class product manager that either can do pretty much anything or can figure out how to get it done. You must have an insane attention to detail, love learning/research, and be focused on making decisions with the best available data. You will be joining a top team and will be taking a serious leadership position with us.<p>To apply, send an email to team at <em>agent</em>inbox.com with \u201cProduct Manager\u201d in the subject."},"story_title":{"matchLevel":"none","matchedWords":[],"value":"Ask HN: Who is hiring? (August 2015)"}},"_tags":["comment","author_agentinbox","story_9996333"],"author":"agentinbox","comment_text":"Agent Inbox | <a href=\"http:&#x2F;&#x2F;agentinbox.com\" rel=\"nofollow\">http:&#x2F;&#x2F;agentinbox.com</a> | Remote (US Based)<p>Product Manager<p>Agent Inbox is transforming the way real estate agents transact business and communicate with one another. We have automated the messaging, scheduling, routing, and other parts of the real estate transaction. We are a product-driven company that is obsessed with the user experience and delighting our customers. We are having tremendous success in our initial markets, have a huge sales pipeline, and are aiming to grow fast.<p>We are looking for a world-class product manager that either can do pretty much anything or can figure out how to get it done. You must have an insane attention to detail, love learning&#x2F;research, and be focused on making decisions with the best available data. You will be joining a top team and will be taking a serious leadership position with us.<p>To apply, send an email to team at agentinbox.com with \u201cProduct Manager\u201d in the subject.","created_at":"2015-08-03T15:08:53Z","created_at_i":1438614533,"objectID":"9996432","parent_id":9996333,"story_id":9996333,"story_title":"Ask HN: Who is hiring? (August 2015)","updated_at":"2024-09-19T22:14:33Z"},{"_highlightResult":{"author":{"matchLevel":"none","matchedWords":[],"value":"olavk"},"comment_text":{"fullyHighlighted":false,"matchLevel":"full","matchedWords":["agent"],"value":"You are comparing apples to oranges. Semantic HTML is important because it is a publicly defined semantics and various consumers and user <em>agent</em>s are programmed against this semantics. Semantics in class-names, the choice of inline styles vs style sheet etc. are purely for maintainability, e.g. you don't reduce accessibility for anybody if don't use semantic class names, at worst you make it more difficult for yourself, but that might depend on your workflow etc."},"story_title":{"matchLevel":"none","matchedWords":[],"value":"\u201cGoogles 'vertical center div css' for the 100th time. reads for 7 minutes\u201d"},"story_url":{"matchLevel":"none","matchedWords":[],"value":"http://www.bleonard.com/blog/2015/08/01/teaching-css/"}},"_tags":["comment","author_olavk","story_9993171"],"author":"olavk","children":[9996284],"comment_text":"You are comparing apples to oranges. Semantic HTML is important because it is a publicly defined semantics and various consumers and user agents are programmed against this semantics. Semantics in class-names, the choice of inline styles vs style sheet etc. are purely for maintainability, e.g. you don&#x27;t reduce accessibility for anybody if don&#x27;t use semantic class names, at worst you make it more difficult for yourself, but that might depend on your workflow etc.","created_at":"2015-08-03T13:42:04Z","created_at_i":1438609324,"objectID":"9995680","parent_id":9995561,"story_id":9993171,"story_title":"\u201cGoogles 'vertical center div css' for the 100th time. reads for 7 minutes\u201d","story_url":"http://www.bleonard.com/blog/2015/08/01/teaching-css/","updated_at":"2024-09-19T22:14:28Z"},{"_highlightResult":{"author":{"matchLevel":"none","matchedWords":[],"value":"grayrest"},"comment_text":{"fullyHighlighted":false,"matchLevel":"full","matchedWords":["agent"],"value":"One of these days I'll remember that <em>agent</em>s aren't actors, just not today."},"story_title":{"matchLevel":"none","matchedWords":[],"value":"Ongoing \u00b7 Concur.next \u2014 Hard-Core Clojure"},"story_url":{"matchLevel":"none","matchedWords":[],"value":"http://www.tbray.org/ongoing/When/200x/2009/12/15/Osborne-WF2-Clojure"}},"_tags":["comment","author_grayrest","story_998796"],"author":"grayrest","comment_text":"One of these days I'll remember that agents aren't actors, just not today.","created_at":"2009-12-16T19:39:25Z","created_at_i":1260992365,"objectID":"999561","parent_id":998957,"story_id":998796,"story_title":"Ongoing \u00b7 Concur.next \u2014 Hard-Core Clojure","story_url":"http://www.tbray.org/ongoing/When/200x/2009/12/15/Osborne-WF2-Clojure","updated_at":"2024-09-19T16:53:57Z"},{"_highlightResult":{"author":{"matchLevel":"none","matchedWords":[],"value":"chrismorgan"},"comment_text":{"fullyHighlighted":false,"matchLevel":"full","matchedWords":["agent"],"value":"Things like resource inlining are an antipattern in an HTTP/2 world. The stylesheet for example <i>should not be inlined</i>; the server should instead push the stylesheet out to the user <em>agent</em> proactively (typically three frames\u2014a PUSH_PROMISE telling the client of the request that is being simulated, then a HEADERS and a DATA frame with the response).<p>The first time, the browser will receive it approximately as fast as the inlined version; subsequent times, there is no overhead, moreover browsers can load the stylesheet only once rather than needing to load it for every page."},"story_title":{"matchLevel":"none","matchedWords":[],"value":"The Fastest Blog in the World"},"story_url":{"matchLevel":"none","matchedWords":[],"value":"http://jacquesmattheij.com/the-fastest-blog-in-the-world"}},"_tags":["comment","author_chrismorgan","story_9994276"],"author":"chrismorgan","comment_text":"Things like resource inlining are an antipattern in an HTTP&#x2F;2 world. The stylesheet for example <i>should not be inlined</i>; the server should instead push the stylesheet out to the user agent proactively (typically three frames\u2014a PUSH_PROMISE telling the client of the request that is being simulated, then a HEADERS and a DATA frame with the response).<p>The first time, the browser will receive it approximately as fast as the inlined version; subsequent times, there is no overhead, moreover browsers can load the stylesheet only once rather than needing to load it for every page.","created_at":"2015-08-03T10:14:36Z","created_at_i":1438596876,"objectID":"9994792","parent_id":9994573,"story_id":9994276,"story_title":"The Fastest Blog in the World","story_url":"http://jacquesmattheij.com/the-fastest-blog-in-the-world","updated_at":"2024-09-19T22:14:22Z"},{"_highlightResult":{"author":{"matchLevel":"none","matchedWords":[],"value":"gioele"},"comment_text":{"fullyHighlighted":false,"matchLevel":"full","matchedWords":["agent"],"value":"Because it <i>is not</i> a table, it <i>displays</i> in a tabular fashion (for certain user <em>agent</em>s).<p>I always failed to understand what is hard about the _being_ something vs _being displayed_ as something. I have met so many smart people just failing to grasp this simple dichotomy.<p>For the sake of public education, here is an example from the article. H1 is for (document) titles, and is so used by auto outliners and Google and Pocket. Document titles are document titles regardless of the way your page is displayed (user <em>agent</em> or current style fashion). If you want to display bigger just use &quot;font-size&quot;."},"story_title":{"matchLevel":"none","matchedWords":[],"value":"\u201cGoogles 'vertical center div css' for the 100th time. reads for 7 minutes\u201d"},"story_url":{"matchLevel":"none","matchedWords":[],"value":"http://www.bleonard.com/blog/2015/08/01/teaching-css/"}},"_tags":["comment","author_gioele","story_9993171"],"author":"gioele","children":[9994167],"comment_text":"Because it <i>is not</i> a table, it <i>displays</i> in a tabular fashion (for certain user agents).<p>I always failed to understand what is hard about the _being_ something vs _being displayed_ as something. I have met so many smart people just failing to grasp this simple dichotomy.<p>For the sake of public education, here is an example from the article. H1 is for (document) titles, and is so used by auto outliners and Google and Pocket. Document titles are document titles regardless of the way your page is displayed (user agent or current style fashion). If you want to display bigger just use &quot;font-size&quot;.","created_at":"2015-08-03T06:12:11Z","created_at_i":1438582331,"objectID":"9994091","parent_id":9993802,"story_id":9993171,"story_title":"\u201cGoogles 'vertical center div css' for the 100th time. reads for 7 minutes\u201d","story_url":"http://www.bleonard.com/blog/2015/08/01/teaching-css/","updated_at":"2024-09-19T22:14:22Z"},{"_highlightResult":{"author":{"matchLevel":"none","matchedWords":[],"value":"afrancis"},"comment_text":{"fullyHighlighted":false,"matchLevel":"full","matchedWords":["agent"],"value":"I don't know much about Zapier but IFTTT seems to me to be more like the infra-structure for software <em>agent</em>s. IFTTT you are still creating recipes. I would like to say that <em>Agent</em> 2.0 would look like the Knowledge Navigator of the Apple videos (<a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=HGYFEI6uLy0\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=HGYFEI6uLy0</a>). Many moons ago, I remember seeing this video in a graduate computer science course on CHI and freaking out. Now the question is what does <em>Agent</em> 1.0 look like?"},"story_title":{"matchLevel":"none","matchedWords":[],"value":"Ask HN: Do you think there will be full replacement to Facebook?"}},"_tags":["comment","author_afrancis","story_9991940"],"author":"afrancis","comment_text":"I don&#x27;t know much about Zapier but IFTTT seems to me to be more like the infra-structure for software agents. IFTTT you are still creating recipes. I would like to say that Agent 2.0 would look like the Knowledge Navigator of the Apple videos (<a href=\"https:&#x2F;&#x2F;www.youtube.com&#x2F;watch?v=HGYFEI6uLy0\" rel=\"nofollow\">https:&#x2F;&#x2F;www.youtube.com&#x2F;watch?v=HGYFEI6uLy0</a>). Many moons ago, I remember seeing this video in a graduate computer science course on CHI and freaking out. Now the question is what does Agent 1.0 look like?","created_at":"2015-08-03T04:25:28Z","created_at_i":1438575928,"objectID":"9993789","parent_id":9992452,"points":null,"story_id":9991940,"story_title":"Ask HN: Do you think there will be full replacement to Facebook?","updated_at":"2023-09-07T03:21:35Z"},{"_highlightResult":{"author":{"matchLevel":"none","matchedWords":[],"value":"franksalim"},"comment_text":{"fullyHighlighted":false,"matchLevel":"full","matchedWords":["agent"],"value":"WebSockets have been capable of cross-origin communication since day one. (see: <a href=\"http://tools.ietf.org/html/draft-hixie-thewebsocketprotocol-66#section-8.4\" rel=\"nofollow\">http://tools.ietf.org/html/draft-hixie-thewebsocketprotocol-...</a>) <i>\"The |WebSocket-Origin| header is used in the Web Socket handshake. It is sent from the server to the client to confirm the origin of the script that opened the connection. This enables user <em>agent</em>s to verify that the server is willing to serve the script that opened the connection.\"</i>"},"story_title":{"matchLevel":"none","matchedWords":[],"value":"Comet is dead, long live websockets"},"story_url":{"matchLevel":"none","matchedWords":[],"value":"http://armstrongonsoftware.blogspot.com/2009/12/comet-is-dead-long-live-websockets.html"}},"_tags":["comment","author_franksalim","story_999135"],"author":"franksalim","children":[999312],"comment_text":"WebSockets have been capable of cross-origin communication since day one. (see: <a href=\"http://tools.ietf.org/html/draft-hixie-thewebsocketprotocol-66#section-8.4\" rel=\"nofollow\">http://tools.ietf.org/html/draft-hixie-thewebsocketprotocol-...</a>) <i>\"The |WebSocket-Origin| header is used in the Web Socket handshake. It is sent from the server to the client to confirm the origin of the script that opened the connection. This enables user agents to verify that the server is willing to serve the script that opened the connection.\"</i>","created_at":"2009-12-16T17:41:27Z","created_at_i":1260985287,"objectID":"999255","parent_id":999195,"story_id":999135,"story_title":"Comet is dead, long live websockets","story_url":"http://armstrongonsoftware.blogspot.com/2009/12/comet-is-dead-long-live-websockets.html","updated_at":"2024-09-19T16:53:57Z"},{"_highlightResult":{"author":{"matchLevel":"none","matchedWords":[],"value":"tuyguntn"},"comment_text":{"fullyHighlighted":false,"matchLevel":"full","matchedWords":["agent"],"value":"I guess Zapier and IFTTT already started the way for software <em>agent</em>s. If we call them <em>Agent</em> 1.0, how do you see <em>Agent</em> 2.0?"},"story_title":{"matchLevel":"none","matchedWords":[],"value":"Ask HN: Do you think there will be full replacement to Facebook?"}},"_tags":["comment","author_tuyguntn","story_9991940"],"author":"tuyguntn","children":[9993789],"comment_text":"I guess Zapier and IFTTT already started the way for software agents. If we call them Agent 1.0, how do you see Agent 2.0?","created_at":"2015-08-02T20:55:25Z","created_at_i":1438548925,"objectID":"9992452","parent_id":9992326,"points":null,"story_id":9991940,"story_title":"Ask HN: Do you think there will be full replacement to Facebook?","updated_at":"2023-09-07T03:21:30Z"},{"_highlightResult":{"author":{"matchLevel":"none","matchedWords":[],"value":"afrancis"},"comment_text":{"fullyHighlighted":false,"matchLevel":"full","matchedWords":["agent"],"value":"Ten to fifty years is a long time to project into the future .... I think there will not be so much a replacement social media web site to Facebook as 1) fragmentation of the social media space. 2) the waning of social media as the predominant focus of personal computing. I would go out on limb and say that software <em>agent</em>s will be the next big thing. That is applications that know a lot about you and do things on your behalf without your direct intervention. Less interaction, not more. I think the proliferation of web APIs  and big data, make software <em>agent</em>s more viable."},"story_title":{"matchLevel":"none","matchedWords":[],"value":"Ask HN: Do you think there will be full replacement to Facebook?"}},"_tags":["comment","author_afrancis","story_9991940"],"author":"afrancis","children":[9992452,9994229],"comment_text":"Ten to fifty years is a long time to project into the future .... I think there will not be so much a replacement social media web site to Facebook as 1) fragmentation of the social media space. 2) the waning of social media as the predominant focus of personal computing. I would go out on limb and say that software agents will be the next big thing. That is applications that know a lot about you and do things on your behalf without your direct intervention. Less interaction, not more. I think the proliferation of web APIs  and big data, make software agents more viable.","created_at":"2015-08-02T20:29:27Z","created_at_i":1438547367,"objectID":"9992326","parent_id":9991940,"points":null,"story_id":9991940,"story_title":"Ask HN: Do you think there will be full replacement to Facebook?","updated_at":"2023-09-07T03:21:30Z"},{"_highlightResult":{"author":{"matchLevel":"none","matchedWords":[],"value":"sleazebreeze"},"comment_text":{"fullyHighlighted":false,"matchLevel":"full","matchedWords":["agent"],"value":"Isn't this basically the plot of Million Dollar Baby or Maximus's first fights in Gladiator? The fighter in both movies wins all their fights very quickly. The difference is that in Gladiator, he is told to slow down and give the crowd a spectacle. In Million Dollar Baby, nobody wants to fight her without extra participation money.<p>I wonder what kind of pressure is being applied to Rousey by her manager, <em>agent</em> and fight organizers?"},"story_title":{"matchLevel":"none","matchedWords":[],"value":"Ronda Rousey fights like a statistical outlier"},"story_url":{"matchLevel":"none","matchedWords":[],"value":"http://fivethirtyeight.com/datalab/ronda-rousey-fights-like-an-outlier/"}},"_tags":["comment","author_sleazebreeze","story_9990758"],"author":"sleazebreeze","children":[9992389],"comment_text":"Isn&#x27;t this basically the plot of Million Dollar Baby or Maximus&#x27;s first fights in Gladiator? The fighter in both movies wins all their fights very quickly. The difference is that in Gladiator, he is told to slow down and give the crowd a spectacle. In Million Dollar Baby, nobody wants to fight her without extra participation money.<p>I wonder what kind of pressure is being applied to Rousey by her manager, agent and fight organizers?","created_at":"2015-08-02T18:11:57Z","created_at_i":1438539117,"objectID":"9991659","parent_id":9990758,"points":null,"story_id":9990758,"story_title":"Ronda Rousey fights like a statistical outlier","story_url":"http://fivethirtyeight.com/datalab/ronda-rousey-fights-like-an-outlier/","updated_at":"2023-09-07T03:21:25Z"},{"_highlightResult":{"author":{"matchLevel":"none","matchedWords":[],"value":"Sami_Lehtinen"},"comment_text":{"fullyHighlighted":false,"matchLevel":"full","matchedWords":["agent"],"value":"No good clients? I loved Forte <em>Agent</em>, it was awesome. As well as it was one of the most bug free programs I've ever encountered. It just worked. <a href=\"http://www.forteinc.com/agent/index.php\" rel=\"nofollow\">http://www.forteinc.com/<em>agent</em>/index.php</a>"},"story_title":{"matchLevel":"none","matchedWords":[],"value":"Ask HN: What was Usenet's ultimate demise?"}},"_tags":["comment","author_Sami_Lehtinen","story_9987679"],"author":"Sami_Lehtinen","comment_text":"No good clients? I loved Forte Agent, it was awesome. As well as it was one of the most bug free programs I&#x27;ve ever encountered. It just worked. <a href=\"http:&#x2F;&#x2F;www.forteinc.com&#x2F;agent&#x2F;index.php\" rel=\"nofollow\">http:&#x2F;&#x2F;www.forteinc.com&#x2F;agent&#x2F;index.php</a>","created_at":"2015-08-02T15:03:13Z","created_at_i":1438527793,"objectID":"9990949","parent_id":9987679,"story_id":9987679,"story_title":"Ask HN: What was Usenet's ultimate demise?","updated_at":"2024-09-19T22:13:51Z"},{"_highlightResult":{"author":{"matchLevel":"none","matchedWords":[],"value":"hodwik"},"comment_text":{"fullyHighlighted":false,"matchLevel":"full","matchedWords":["agent"],"value":"Teeth whitening is very cheap, you can buy teeth whiteners over the counter in the US, and most toothpastes you can buy in the store have whitening <em>agent</em>s in them."},"story_title":{"matchLevel":"none","matchedWords":[],"value":"Teeth Whitening and the Hygiene Hypothesis"},"story_url":{"matchLevel":"none","matchedWords":[],"value":"http://nautil.us/issue/26/color/have-we-hit-peak-whiteness-rd"}},"_tags":["comment","author_hodwik","story_9989806"],"author":"hodwik","children":[9990885,9991893],"comment_text":"Teeth whitening is very cheap, you can buy teeth whiteners over the counter in the US, and most toothpastes you can buy in the store have whitening agents in them.","created_at":"2015-08-02T14:40:18Z","created_at_i":1438526418,"objectID":"9990872","parent_id":9990602,"story_id":9989806,"story_title":"Teeth Whitening and the Hygiene Hypothesis","story_url":"http://nautil.us/issue/26/color/have-we-hit-peak-whiteness-rd","updated_at":"2024-09-19T22:13:51Z"},{"_highlightResult":{"author":{"matchLevel":"none","matchedWords":[],"value":"logicuce"},"comment_text":{"fullyHighlighted":false,"matchLevel":"full","matchedWords":["agent"],"value":"For your need to simulate a 256kbps connection, two things have worked for me. Both require a good few mbps connection to begin with though:<p>1. Use Chrome's device emulator mode. You can ignore all other settings like screen size, user <em>agent</em>, etc. and just use the speed restriction.\n2. Use a specialized WiFi router. I use the ones from TP-Link in which I can restrict speed for a particular device IP. DD WRT based routers can also help here."},"story_title":{"matchLevel":"none","matchedWords":[],"value":"Ask HN: Why and how is Hacker News so fast?"}},"_tags":["comment","author_logicuce","story_9990630"],"author":"logicuce","children":[9990837],"comment_text":"For your need to simulate a 256kbps connection, two things have worked for me. Both require a good few mbps connection to begin with though:<p>1. Use Chrome&#x27;s device emulator mode. You can ignore all other settings like screen size, user agent, etc. and just use the speed restriction.\n2. Use a specialized WiFi router. I use the ones from TP-Link in which I can restrict speed for a particular device IP. DD WRT based routers can also help here.","created_at":"2015-08-02T14:02:07Z","created_at_i":1438524127,"objectID":"9990753","parent_id":9990630,"story_id":9990630,"story_title":"Ask HN: Why and how is Hacker News so fast?","updated_at":"2024-09-19T22:13:51Z"},{"_highlightResult":{"author":{"matchLevel":"none","matchedWords":[],"value":"qbrass"},"comment_text":{"fullyHighlighted":false,"matchLevel":"full","matchedWords":["agent"],"value":"<em>Agent</em>s interact with their environment while actors interact with other actors.<p>If one actor isn't aware of another actor, it can't send a message to them. An <em>agent</em> can broadcast a message through the environment, and any other <em>agent</em>s who notice can respond.<p>You could turn <em>agent</em>s into actors by limiting what they respond to, and you can turn actors into <em>agent</em>s, by having an environment actor and <em>agent</em> actors."},"story_title":{"fullyHighlighted":false,"matchLevel":"full","matchedWords":["agent"],"value":"SARL \u2013\u00a0General-purpose <em>Agent</em>-Oriented Programming Language"},"story_url":{"matchLevel":"none","matchedWords":[],"value":"http://www.sarl.io/"}},"_tags":["comment","author_qbrass","story_9988853"],"author":"qbrass","comment_text":"Agents interact with their environment while actors interact with other actors.<p>If one actor isn&#x27;t aware of another actor, it can&#x27;t send a message to them. An agent can broadcast a message through the environment, and any other agents who notice can respond.<p>You could turn agents into actors by limiting what they respond to, and you can turn actors into agents, by having an environment actor and agent actors.","created_at":"2015-08-02T11:57:09Z","created_at_i":1438516629,"objectID":"9990470","parent_id":9990005,"story_id":9988853,"story_title":"SARL \u2013\u00a0General-purpose Agent-Oriented Programming Language","story_url":"http://www.sarl.io/","updated_at":"2024-09-19T22:13:51Z"},{"_highlightResult":{"author":{"matchLevel":"none","matchedWords":[],"value":"veli_joza"},"comment_text":{"fullyHighlighted":false,"matchLevel":"full","matchedWords":["agent"],"value":"I have zero experience with <em>agent</em>s, can someone explain how different this language is from Erlang? Aside from syntax, obviously.<p>The concept of <em>agent</em> capabilities composition reminds me of entity-component-system paradigm, except that there's no data encapsulation in ECS. Perhaps <em>agent</em>-oriented design could be successfully applied to game programming?"},"story_title":{"fullyHighlighted":false,"matchLevel":"full","matchedWords":["agent"],"value":"SARL \u2013\u00a0General-purpose <em>Agent</em>-Oriented Programming Language"},"story_url":{"matchLevel":"none","matchedWords":[],"value":"http://www.sarl.io/"}},"_tags":["comment","author_veli_joza","story_9988853"],"author":"veli_joza","children":[9990470],"comment_text":"I have zero experience with agents, can someone explain how different this language is from Erlang? Aside from syntax, obviously.<p>The concept of agent capabilities composition reminds me of entity-component-system paradigm, except that there&#x27;s no data encapsulation in ECS. Perhaps agent-oriented design could be successfully applied to game programming?","created_at":"2015-08-02T06:41:29Z","created_at_i":1438497689,"objectID":"9990005","parent_id":9988853,"story_id":9988853,"story_title":"SARL \u2013\u00a0General-purpose Agent-Oriented Programming Language","story_url":"http://www.sarl.io/","updated_at":"2024-09-19T22:13:51Z"},{"_highlightResult":{"author":{"matchLevel":"none","matchedWords":[],"value":"pmjordan"},"comment_text":{"fullyHighlighted":false,"matchLevel":"full","matchedWords":["agent"],"value":"<em>Agent</em>s launch the update function in a separate thread, which seems a bit much for incrementing a counter."},"story_title":{"matchLevel":"none","matchedWords":[],"value":"Ongoing \u00b7 Concur.next \u2014 Hard-Core Clojure"},"story_url":{"matchLevel":"none","matchedWords":[],"value":"http://www.tbray.org/ongoing/When/200x/2009/12/15/Osborne-WF2-Clojure"}},"_tags":["comment","author_pmjordan","story_998796"],"author":"pmjordan","children":[999561],"comment_text":"Agents launch the update function in a separate thread, which seems a bit much for incrementing a counter.","created_at":"2009-12-16T15:42:46Z","created_at_i":1260978166,"objectID":"998957","parent_id":998875,"story_id":998796,"story_title":"Ongoing \u00b7 Concur.next \u2014 Hard-Core Clojure","story_url":"http://www.tbray.org/ongoing/When/200x/2009/12/15/Osborne-WF2-Clojure","updated_at":"2024-09-19T16:53:52Z"}],"hitsPerPage":25,"nbHits":640785,"nbPages":40,"page":0,"params":"query=agent&tags=comment&hitsPerPage=25&advancedSyntax=true&analyticsTags=backend","processingTimeMS":88,"processingTimingsMS":{"_request":{"queue":22,"roundTrip":16},"afterFetch":{"format":{"highlighting":1,"total":2},"merge":{"mergeLoop":{"prepareNextHit":1,"total":1},"total":1},"total":1},"fetch":{"query":8,"scanning":77,"total":86},"total":88},"query":"agent","serverTimeMS":113}
